DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261005
SUMMARY:✓ Long run · 29 km rolling hills
DESCRIPTION:Done: 29.0 km in 2:37:48\, +219 m. 24 km at 5:35/km (avg HR abo
 ut 130)\, then 5 km at 4:18/km\, quickening from 4:24 to 4:13 (HR 153–16
 8). 5 gels\, stomach fine. Felt really good\n\nStrava: 29 km at 5:26/km\, 
 avg HR 135\n\n• 5:30–5:45/km for the first 24 km\, HR under 150\n• L
 ast 5 km at 4:20/km only if your legs have recovered from Tuesday. Otherwi
 se stay easy\n• Run the hills by effort\, not pace\n\nWhy: Builds time o
 n your feet and starts training your gut to take race fuel.\n\nFuel: Gut t
 raining starts here. Eat your planned race breakfast 2.5–3 h before. Tak
 e a gel every 25 min from 25 min in (about 6)\, each with water. That's ab
 out 60 g of carbs per hour.\n\nHeart rate guide (estimated from your recen
 t runs\, may be off):\n• 5:30–5:45/km: easy\, HR 125–150. Over 150 m
 eans slow down\n• 4:17–4:23/km: HR about 158–170\n\nhttps://joshuamo
 rley.github.io/running-plan/#plan
URL:https://joshuamorley.github.io/running-plan/#plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
