BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:akl-2026-10-10@joshuamorley.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261028T215149Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261011
SUMMARY:✓ Long run · 33 km · Test 1
DESCRIPTION:Done: 33.0 km in 2:54:07\, +35 m. 25 km at 5:36/km (avg HR abou
 t 144)\, then 8 km at 4:15/km\, last 2 km at 4:11 (HR 167–181\, max 185)
 . 6 gels about every 22 min\, caffeine in the last 2. A little sloshing th
 at settled quickly\n\nStrava: 33 km at 5:17/km\, avg HR 150\n\n• First 2
 5 km easy at 5:30–5:45/km\n• Last 8 km at 4:15/km\, your sub-3 race pa
 ce\n• Note your average pace and HR over the last 8 km\, and whether the
  final 2–3 km slowed\n• If you slow by more than 10 s/km\, ease back t
 o easy and jog it home. That's your answer for Decision 2\n\nWhy: Sub-3 pa
 ce on tired legs is the closest you can get to the last 10 km of the race.
 \n\nFuel: Full race rehearsal. Race breakfast 3 h before\, a gel 10–15 m
 in before you start\, then gels on your race schedule (see the Fuel tab)\,
  each with water. Use your race-day flavour mix: non-caffeine early\, caff
 eine gels from about km 18.\n\nHeart rate guide (estimated from your recen
 t runs\, may be off):\n• 5:30–5:45/km: easy\, HR 125–150. Over 150 m
 eans slow down\n• 4:13–4:17/km: HR about 158–170\n\nhttps://joshuamo
 rley.github.io/running-plan/#plan
URL:https://joshuamorley.github.io/running-plan/#plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:akl-2026-10-13@joshuamorley.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261028T215149Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261013
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261014
SUMMARY:✓ Tuesday 5k · steady · 5 km
DESCRIPTION:Strava: 5 km at 4:09/km\, avg HR 162\n\n• Around 4:00–4:10/
 km. Controlled\, not a race\n• Expect HR about 165–175\, creeping up i
 n the last km or two\n• If HR is past 178 before 4 km\, ease off. That's
  race effort\, and Sunday matters more\n\nWhy: Keeps your legs sharp witho
 ut taking anything out of them for Sunday.\n\nFuel: None needed. Eat a nor
 mal carb-based meal afterwards.\n\nHeart rate guide (estimated from your r
 ecent runs\, may be off):\n• 4:00–4:10/km: HR about 165–175\n\nRUN G
 UIDE\n\nHow it should feel: Comfortably hard. You can say a few words but 
 wouldn't want to chat. Smooth and in control\, never straining.\n\nHow to 
 run it:\n• Jog 1–2 km beforehand and do 2–3 strides\n• Km 1 at 4:1
 0. Don't go out with the racers\n• Km 2–4 settle at 4:00–4:05\n• K
 m 5 hold the pace. No sprint finish\n\nHeart rate:\n• Expect about 165
 –175\, creeping up in the last km or two\n• The 33 km may still be in 
 your legs\, and a warm evening adds 3–5 bpm\n\nElevation: Flat. Under 20
  m of climbing\, like the Good George course (+5 m) or your usual morning 
 loop.\n\nBack off if:\n• HR past 178 before 4 km: ease to 4:15\n• Any 
 niggle from Saturday: jog it easy and call it a recovery run\n\nAfterwards
 : Jog 1 km to cool down. Normal dinner. Tomorrow is rest or an easy 30 min
 .\n\nhttps://joshuamorley.github.io/running-plan/#plan
URL:https://joshuamorley.github.io/running-plan/#plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:akl-2026-10-14@joshuamorley.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261028T215149Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261014
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261015
SUMMARY:✓ Easy run · 5 km
DESCRIPTION:Strava: 5 km at 5:33/km\, avg HR 141\n\n• 5:20–5:45/km. Kee
 p it short before Sunday.\n\nWhy: Easy volume\, nothing more.\n\nFuel: Non
 e needed. Eat a normal carb-based meal afterwards.\n\nHeart rate guide (es
 timated from your recent runs\, may be off):\n• 5:20–5:45/km: easy\, H
 R 125–150. Over 150 means slow down\n\nRUN GUIDE\n\nHow it should feel: 
 Very easy. Full sentences the whole way. This only adds volume\, so it sho
 uld feel like nothing.\n\nHow to run it:\n• 5:20–5:45/km from the firs
 t step\n• Skip it if your legs are heavy after last night\n\nElevation: 
 Anything gentle\, up to about 40 m. Walk any steep pinch rather than pushi
 ng.\n\nBack off if:\n• HR over 150: slow down\n• Tight calves or hamst
 rings: stop and walk home. Sunday matters more\n\nAfterwards: Nothing spec
 ial. Normal meals.\n\nhttps://joshuamorley.github.io/running-plan/#plan
URL:https://joshuamorley.github.io/running-plan/#plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:akl-2026-10-15@joshuamorley.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261028T215149Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:✓ Morning intervals · light · 9.5 km
DESCRIPTION:Strava: 9.6 km at 4:41/km\, avg HR 157\n\n• 2 km easy warm-up
 \n• 4 × 1 km at 3:50/km\, 2 min jog between\n• 2 km easy cool-down\n\
 nWhy: Sharpens you up without tiring you before the test.\n\nFuel: None du
 ring. Have carbs and protein within an hour afterwards.\n\nHeart rate guid
 e (estimated from your recent runs\, may be off):\n• 5:20–5:45/km: eas
 y\, HR 125–150. Over 150 means slow down\n• 3:48–3:52/km: HR about 1
 72–182\n\nRUN GUIDE\n\nHow it should feel: Reps feel strong and quick bu
 t relaxed\, like the middle of a 10k race. You finish wanting one more.\n\
 nHow to run it:\n• 2 km easy\, then 3–4 strides\n• 4 × 1 km at 3:48
 –3:52/km. Rep 1 at 3:52\, then settle\n• 2 min easy jog between\, not 
 a walk\n• 2 km easy cool-down\n\nHeart rate:\n• HR won't settle in a 1
  km rep. Run by pace and breathing\n• Expect the end of each rep around 
 170–178\n\nElevation: Flat. Under 20 m of climbing\, like the Good Georg
 e course (+5 m) or your usual morning loop. Do the reps on the flattest st
 retch you have\, so the paces mean something.\n\nBack off if:\n• If a re
 p is more than 5 s slower than rep 1\, stop there\n• Three days before t
 he test\, so leave something in the tank\n\nAfterwards: Carbs and protein 
 within an hour. Rest tomorrow.\n\nhttps://joshuamorley.github.io/running-p
 lan/#plan
URL:https://joshuamorley.github.io/running-plan/#plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:akl-2026-10-17@joshuamorley.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261028T215149Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
SUMMARY:✓ Easy run + strides · 5 km
DESCRIPTION:Strava: 5.5 km at 5:16/km\, avg HR 139\n\n• 5:30/km easy\, th
 en 4 × 20 s relaxed strides.\n\nWhy: Strides wake your legs up for tomorr
 ow.\n\nFuel: Carb-heavy dinner tonight.\n\nHeart rate guide (estimated fro
 m your recent runs\, may be off):\n• 5:25–5:35/km: easy\, HR 125–150
 . Over 150 means slow down\n\nRUN GUIDE\n\nHow it should feel: Loose and e
 asy\, with the strides feeling quick and light\, not sprinting.\n\nHow to 
 run it:\n• 4.5 km at about 5:30/km\n• 4 × 20 s strides: build to abou
 t 3:30/km pace\, stay tall and relaxed\n• 60 s walk or jog between strid
 es\n\nElevation: Flat. Under 20 m of climbing\, like the Good George cours
 e (+5 m) or your usual morning loop.\n\nBack off if:\n• Anything tight: 
 skip the strides\n\nAfterwards: Carb-heavy dinner. Lay out your kit and ge
 ls for tomorrow. Early night.\n\nhttps://joshuamorley.github.io/running-pl
 an/#plan
URL:https://joshuamorley.github.io/running-plan/#plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:akl-2026-10-18@joshuamorley.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261028T215149Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261018
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
SUMMARY:✓ Half marathon · Test 2 · 21.1 km
DESCRIPTION:Done: 21.1 km in 1:31:16\, a half marathon best. 16 km at 4:14/
 km (every km 4:12–4:17)\, avg HR 164\, max 171\, settling from 167 to ab
 out 164 after km 8. Then 5 km at 4:35/km (HR 153–159). Felt comfortable 
 and fuelling was fine. Sub-3 stays the target\n\nStrava: 22.6 km at 4:26/k
 m\, avg HR 160\n\n• Your dress rehearsal: full race kit and shoes\, race
  breakfast 3 h before\, gels on schedule\n• Run it as a controlled train
 ing run\, not a race. Two weeks out is too close to race a half\n• First
  16 km at 4:15/km\n• Last 5 km easy to steady\, 4:45–5:15/km. Don't sp
 eed up\n• If HR goes past 170 before 16 km\, ease off. That tells you so
 mething useful\, it isn't a failure\n• Note your average pace and HR ove
 r the first 16 km\, and whether you could have kept going\n\nWhy: The best
  guide to your race pace you'll get before race day\, without taking so mu
 ch out of you that it hurts the marathon.\n\nFuel: Race-day routine: break
 fast 3 h before\, a gel 10–15 min before the start\, then gels at about 
 km 6\, 11 and 17\, each with water.\n\nHeart rate guide (estimated from yo
 ur recent runs\, may be off):\n• 4:13–4:17/km: HR about 158–170\n•
  4:45–5:15/km: steady\, HR about 140–158\n\nRUN GUIDE\n\nHow it should
  feel: 4:15 should feel controlled and rhythmic\, like marathon effort\, n
 ot half-marathon effort. The first 10 km should feel almost easy.\n\nHow t
 o run it:\n• Dress rehearsal: full race kit and shoes\, race breakfast 3
  h before\, ideally at the time you'd eat it on race day\n• 1–2 km eas
 y warm-up and a few strides\n• Km 1–16 at 4:13–4:17. Lock in by km 2
  and don't bank time\n• Km 17–21 at 4:45–5:15. Don't speed up even i
 f you feel great\n\nHeart rate:\n• At 4:15 expect about 158–170\, drif
 ting up slowly\n• Your 33 km had the last 8 km at 4:15 at HR 167–181\,
  but that was on tired legs. Fresh\, it should be lower\n\nElevation: If y
 ou're picking the route\, aim for about 80–150 m of climbing. That's abo
 ut the race's climbing per km (roughly 5 m/km\, plus a bit for the bridge)
 \, so the test is honest. Put one longer climb in the first half\, like th
 e bridge. Run hills by effort\, not pace.\n\nBack off if:\n• HR past 170
  before 16 km: ease off and note when it happened\n• 4:15 feels forced b
 y km 8: drop to 4:30 and finish as the 4:30 test\n• Any sharp pain: stop
 . A missed test beats a missed race\n\nAfterwards: Write down your average
  pace and HR over the first 16 km\, and whether you could have kept going.
  Carbs and protein within an hour. Then pick your target on the Decisions 
 tab.\n\nhttps://joshuamorley.github.io/running-plan/#plan
URL:https://joshuamorley.github.io/running-plan/#plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:akl-2026-10-20@joshuamorley.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261028T215149Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261020
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261021
SUMMARY:✓ Tuesday 5k · last sharp one · 5 km
DESCRIPTION:Strava: 7.1 km at 4:24/km\, avg HR 156\n\n• Race it if you wa
 nt. Twelve days out is fine. Otherwise run it at threshold.\n\nWhy: One la
 st effort to stay sharp\, with 12 days left to recover.\n\nFuel: None duri
 ng. Have carbs and protein within an hour afterwards.\n\nHeart rate guide 
 (estimated from your recent runs\, may be off):\n• Race effort: HR climb
 s past 180 (your 5k averaged 184). Run it by feel\n\nRUN GUIDE\n\nHow it s
 hould feel: If you race it: hard\, like the 29 Sep 5k. If not: threshold\,
  comfortably hard and even.\n\nHow to run it:\n• Jog 1–2 km and do 3
 –4 strides\n• Racing: km 1 no faster than 3:35\, then hold. Your 17:44
  averaged 3:33\n• Threshold: 3:50–4:00/km the whole way\n\nHeart rate:
 \n• Racing: expect 180+ by km 3\n• Threshold: about 172–180\n\nEleva
 tion: Flat. Under 20 m of climbing\, like the Good George course (+5 m) or
  your usual morning loop.\n\nBack off if:\n• Any niggle from Sunday: run
  it easy. Twelve days out\, nothing is gained by forcing it\n\nAfterwards:
  Carbs and protein within an hour. Rest tomorrow.\n\nhttps://joshuamorley.
 github.io/running-plan/#plan
URL:https://joshuamorley.github.io/running-plan/#plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:akl-2026-10-22@joshuamorley.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261028T215149Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261022
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261023
SUMMARY:✓ Morning intervals · pace + speed · 10 km
DESCRIPTION:Strava: 10.1 km at 4:45/km\, avg HR 155\n\n• 2 km easy warm-u
 p\n• 4 km at 4:15/km\n• 4 × 400 m at 3:35/km\, 200 m jog between\n•
  1.5 km easy cool-down\n• Race shoes and race kit. This replaces the Sun
 day race practice\n\nWhy: Your last proper race-pace run before race week\
 , so it takes a little of the dropped race practice. The 400s keep some po
 p in your legs.\n\nFuel: None during. Have carbs and protein within an hou
 r afterwards.\n\nHeart rate guide (estimated from your recent runs\, may b
 e off):\n• 5:20–5:45/km: easy\, HR 125–150. Over 150 means slow down
 \n• 4:13–4:17/km: HR about 158–170\n• 3:32–3:38/km: too short fo
 r HR to settle. Run these by pace\n\nRUN GUIDE\n\nHow it should feel: The 
 4 km at race pace should feel smooth and easy enough to hold for 42 km. Th
 e 400s feel quick and springy\, not a sprint.\n\nHow to run it:\n• Race 
 shoes and race kit\n• 2 km easy\n• 4 km at 4:13–4:17/km. Practise ex
 actly how race pace feels\n• 4 × 400 m at 3:32–3:38/km\, 200 m jog be
 tween\n• 1.5 km easy cool-down\n\nHeart rate:\n• At race pace expect a
 bout 158–170 by the end of the 4 km. Note it\, it's your race-day number
 \n• 400s are too short for HR to mean much. Run by pace\n\nElevation: Fl
 at. Under 20 m of climbing\, like the Good George course (+5 m) or your us
 ual morning loop. Race pace on the flat is what you're memorising.\n\nBack
  off if:\n• If race pace feels hard today\, skip the 400s. You need rest
 \, not more work\n\nAfterwards: Carbs and protein within an hour. Note any
 thing that rubbed or annoyed you in your race kit\, and fix it before race
  week.\n\nhttps://joshuamorley.github.io/running-plan/#plan
URL:https://joshuamorley.github.io/running-plan/#plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
