DTSTAMP:20261028T215149Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261026
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261027
SUMMARY:Easy evening run · 5 km
DESCRIPTION:• 5:30–5:45/km. Moved from Friday. Keep it short.\n\nWhy: L
 oosens the legs after four days off\, ahead of Tuesday's 5k.\n\nFuel: None
  needed. Eat a normal carb-based meal afterwards.\n\nHeart rate guide (est
 imated from your recent runs\, may be off):\n• 5:30–5:45/km: easy\, HR
  125–150. Over 150 means slow down\n\nRUN GUIDE\n\nHow it should feel: E
 asy and relaxed. Full sentences the whole way. Legs may feel stale after t
 he weekend off. That's normal.\n\nHow to run it:\n• 5:30–5:45/km from 
 the first step\n• 25–30 minutes is plenty\n\nElevation: Anything gentl
 e\, up to about 50 m.\n\nBack off if:\n• HR over 150: slow down\n• Any
 thing tight: cut it to 3 km\n\nAfterwards: Nothing special. Easy 5k tomorr
 ow.\n\nhttps://joshuamorley.github.io/running-plan/#plan
URL:https://joshuamorley.github.io/running-plan/#plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
